1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:05,256
Friday evening, in another city, a stranger puts a new SIM card into a new phone.

2
00:00:05,306 --> 00:00:08,952
This afternoon, the mobile operator gave him Aziz's number.

3
00:00:09,002 --> 00:00:12,216
He installs the mobile bank and taps Forgot password.

4
00:00:12,266 --> 00:00:16,632
Every SMS to Aziz's number now arrives on his phone.

5
00:00:16,682 --> 00:00:18,504
Is that enough to take the account?

6
00:00:18,554 --> 00:00:24,504
In Lesson 29, a password change ended every session of the same or a lower rank.

7
00:00:24,554 --> 00:00:30,456
This lesson opens the other door to a new password: the reset, when the person has no session at all.

8
00:00:30,506 --> 00:00:33,600
A reset in the master app starts with the phone number.

9
00:00:33,650 --> 00:00:37,968
Then the platform runs the checks of a login from that phone, without the password.

10
00:00:38,018 --> 00:00:42,000
On a known phone, that is a one-time code through TAF.

11
00:00:42,050 --> 00:00:47,640
On a new phone, it is the new-device code through TAF, and then the account check.

12
00:00:47,690 --> 00:00:49,512
Watch the stranger.

13
00:00:49,562 --> 00:00:54,744
The TAF code arrives on his phone, because the SIM card really has Aziz's number.

14
00:00:54,794 --> 00:00:56,424
The verdict can even be green.

15
00:00:56,474 --> 00:01:01,464
But Aziz was at level two, so the account check asks for MyID on this new phone.

16
00:01:01,514 --> 00:01:06,000
The stranger's face is not Aziz's face, and the reset stops.

17
00:01:06,050 --> 00:01:07,968
MyID protects Aziz.

18
00:01:08,018 --> 00:01:10,944
But what about a customer who was never at level two?

19
00:01:10,994 --> 00:01:13,176
There is no face on file to compare.

20
00:01:13,226 --> 00:01:16,512
For that customer, a second guard does the work: time.

21
00:01:16,562 --> 00:01:22,632
When the person still has an active session somewhere, the reset does not change the password at once.

22
00:01:22,682 --> 00:01:24,936
It waits for the configured waiting period.

23
00:01:24,986 --> 00:01:28,392
The platform answers with the time when the reset will end.

24
00:01:28,442 --> 00:01:35,400
And it sends a notification, password reset requested, by push to every session and by SMS.

25
00:01:35,450 --> 00:01:38,304
The real owner sees it on the phone in his pocket.

26
00:01:38,354 --> 00:01:41,616
Now only two parties can cancel the waiting reset.

27
00:01:41,666 --> 00:01:47,112
One is a session of rank two: a master-app session with a green TAF check.

28
00:01:47,162 --> 00:01:49,800
The other is a bank operator, with a reason.

29
00:01:49,850 --> 00:01:53,712
A session of rank one gets the notification, but no cancel button.

30
00:01:53,762 --> 00:01:55,584
Why so strict?

31
00:01:55,634 --> 00:02:00,384
A cancel keeps the old password alive, so only the strongest check may do it.

32
00:02:00,434 --> 00:02:06,816
When the owner taps Cancel, the old password stays valid, and a notification says that the reset was cancelled.

33
00:02:06,866 --> 00:02:09,936
When nobody cancels, the waiting period ends.

34
00:02:09,986 --> 00:02:13,632
The new password becomes valid, and the phone gets a session.

35
00:02:13,682 --> 00:02:19,008
Every other session of the same or a lower rank ends, and the probation period starts.

36
00:02:19,058 --> 00:02:21,816
Then the notification: password changed.

37
00:02:21,866 --> 00:02:26,496
I think this waiting reset is the most important rule against a SIM swap.

38
00:02:26,546 --> 00:02:31,224
An SMS code alone must never take an account from a person who is still using it.

39
00:02:31,274 --> 00:02:32,808
Now the honest case.

40
00:02:32,858 --> 00:02:37,800
On Sunday, Aziz himself forgets his password, on his own trusted phone.

41
00:02:37,850 --> 00:02:42,432
The mobile bank sends a code through TAF, and the verdict is green.

42
00:02:42,482 --> 00:02:46,752
Then the mobile bank offers him a MyID check, right inside the reset.

43
00:02:46,802 --> 00:02:48,336
He passes the re-check.

44
00:02:48,386 --> 00:02:52,752
With a green verdict and MyID on this phone, the reset does not wait.

45
00:02:52,802 --> 00:02:56,184
Aziz types a new password, and types it a second time.

46
00:02:56,234 --> 00:02:58,488
That is the deal the master app offers.

47
00:02:58,538 --> 00:03:03,768
Prove the SIM with TAF, and prove the face with MyID, and you skip the wait.

48
00:03:03,818 --> 00:03:09,528
A customer who was never at level two can do the same, with a full MyID check and consent.

49
00:03:09,578 --> 00:03:12,168
Without MyID, the reset waits.

50
00:03:12,218 --> 00:03:18,480
And when the person has no active session at all, there is nobody to warn, so the reset does not wait either.

51
00:03:18,530 --> 00:03:20,352
Now the side apps.

52
00:03:20,402 --> 00:03:25,440
They have no TAF and no MyID, so their reset is weaker.

53
00:03:25,490 --> 00:03:30,960
A side app may reset a password with an SMS code from the bank's SMS service.

54
00:03:31,010 --> 00:03:35,568
But only for a customer with no master-app account, who was never at level two.

55
00:03:35,618 --> 00:03:38,520
Everyone else must reset in the mobile bank.

56
00:03:38,570 --> 00:03:42,912
The side-app reset is limited per day, then a cool-down follows.

57
00:03:42,962 --> 00:03:47,016
And the waiting rule still applies when the customer has an active session.

58
00:03:47,066 --> 00:03:51,936
Yes, a SIM swap is still a risk for a customer who uses only side apps.

59
00:03:51,986 --> 00:03:55,776
The bank accepts that risk, on purpose, and writes it down.

60
00:03:55,826 --> 00:03:57,192
Last, the trail.

61
00:03:57,242 --> 00:04:06,264
Each step of each reset writes an audit event and an antifraud event, and sends a notification to every other session and by SMS.

62
00:04:06,314 --> 00:04:08,832
Resets for each customer are counted, too.

63
00:04:08,882 --> 00:04:14,088
And a bank operator can cancel or approve a waiting reset, always with a reason.

64
00:04:14,138 --> 00:04:19,344
To recap: the master-app reset runs the checks of a login, without the password.

65
00:04:19,394 --> 00:04:25,488
An active session makes the reset wait, and only a rank-two session or an operator can cancel it.

66
00:04:25,538 --> 00:04:29,520
Green TAF and MyID together make it immediate.

67
00:04:29,570 --> 00:04:35,376
And side apps reset by SMS only for customers the master app has never seen.

68
00:04:35,426 --> 00:04:38,328
But go back to the stranger with Aziz's SIM card.

69
00:04:38,378 --> 00:04:40,032
He did not forget the password.

70
00:04:40,082 --> 00:04:43,248
He guessed it, and he tries a normal login on his new phone.

71
00:04:43,298 --> 00:04:46,944
Aziz's phone lights up: Approve, or This was not me.

72
00:04:46,994 --> 00:04:49,272
What happens after he taps This was not me?

73
00:04:49,322 --> 00:04:51,024
Next: this was not me.
